# Identity (FHT-Specification#27): this file describes the FHT *development*
# repository only. It carries no DOI of its own — this repository publishes no
# GitHub releases or tags, the FHT contract itself is not yet released by
# FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification, and no FHT Zenodo or Zenodo-concept record
# exists, so none is implied here. The previously claimed resource identifiers
# (the shared concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.6762549 and the FHR preprint DOI
# 10.1101/2023.11.29.569306) and the FAIR-bioHeaders-Tools repository-code
# target were defects and are removed; the concept DOI identifies the shared
# publication repository's releases, and the preprint is an FHR manuscript.
# The registered bibliographic titles in `references` below ("FAIR-bioHeaders
# Specification") belong to the shared publication lineage; FHT work must not
# rename them, and they do not identify this development repository. Any future
# FHT release record is a maintainer action coordinated through
# FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#107 (FHT lane F of
# FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification#211; publication requires maintainer approval).
#
# Source provenance of the draft contract: fht.json (title "FHT", JSON Schema
# 2020-12, served from the main branch only) was generated from the FHT 1.0
# LinkML model at PR #21 (merge commit 0ceb6f460e1f749f9eb2afb0a8b2f83cddb0e07a)
# and extended with top-level x- keys at PR #24 (commit 2d582f1); it imports the
# pinned shared core snapshot in schemas/provenance.json (commit
# 980029e5886a1a56a2d2545bfe59c7107539d38d, shared v0.4.0/v0.4.1 line). The
# schemaVersion "1.0" value is a development draft, not a released contract:
# FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification v0.5.0 registers only FHR, FHP and FHGFF3 in
# schemas/versions.json, and no https://w3id.org/fair-bioheaders/fht/ alias
# exists.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FHT Specification (development repository)
message: >-
  There is no citable FHT contract yet. This repository develops the FHT
  (transcriptome-set) header of the FAIR BioHeaders family, but no FAIR-
  bioHeaders-Specification release carries an FHT contract, so no FHT version
  DOI, w3id alias or concept record exists and none may be cited. To reference
  the work in progress, cite this development repository URL
  (https://github.com/FAIR-bioHeaders/FHT-Specification) together with the
  draft trail: issue #7 (shared-core integration), PR #21 (FHT 1.0 LinkML model
  and generated draft fht.json) and PR #24 (x- extension fields). The records
  listed under `references` are FHR-lineage publications kept as labeled
  related citations, not FHT identifiers, and nothing here indicates FHT
  adoption or publication. Historical USDA public-domain material remains
  public domain; applicable subsequent project contributions from March 2025
  onward use MPL-2.0. Third-party terms and provenance details are documented
  in LICENSE.
type: dataset
authors:
- given-names: David
  family-names: Molik
  email: molik@fhref.org
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3192-6538
- given-names: Adam
  family-names: Wright
  email: wright@fhref.org
  affiliation: OICR
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5719-4024
# No `identifiers`, `doi`, `version` or `date-released`: this development
# repository publishes no release artifacts or DOI, and the FHT contract is
# unreleased (tracked in FHT-Specification#27; do not borrow the lineage
# records below).
repository-code: https://github.com/FAIR-bioHeaders/FHT-Specification
url: https://github.com/FAIR-bioHeaders/FHT-Specification
abstract: >-
  The FAIR bioHeaders Transcriptome set (FHT) standard embeds a small YAML
  metadata header inside transcriptome FASTA files, validated against a
  per-type JSON Schema contract and covered by a checksum of the file's exact
  bytes. This repository is the FHT development surface: the FHT 1.0 LinkML
  model, the generated draft fht.json contract (JSON Schema 2020-12, pinned to
  the shared core snapshot in schemas/provenance.json), the draft examples and
  the conformance fixtures are developed and served here. FHT is not yet part
  of any FAIR-bioHeaders-Specification release; publication and release DOIs
  remain future maintainer actions.
keywords:
- FAIR
- TRUST
- transcriptome
- transcriptome assembly
- fasta
- yaml
- json
license: MPL-2.0
# Historical permissions and third-party exceptions are documented in LICENSE.
references:
# The motivating family publication; it describes FHR, not FHT.
- type: article
  title: 'FAIR Header Reference genome: a TRUSTworthy standard'
  authors:
  - given-names: Adam
    family-names: Wright
  - given-names: Mark D
    family-names: Wilkinson
  - given-names: Christopher
    family-names: Mungall
  - given-names: Scott
    family-names: Cain
  - given-names: Stephen
    family-names: Richards
  - given-names: Paul
    family-names: Sternberg
  - given-names: Ellen
    family-names: Provin
  - given-names: Jonathan L
    family-names: Jacobs
  - given-names: Scott
    family-names: Geib
  - given-names: Daniela
    family-names: Raciti
  - given-names: Karen
    family-names: Yook
  - given-names: Lincoln
    family-names: Stein
  - given-names: David C
    family-names: Molik
  doi: 10.1093/bib/bbae122
  journal: Briefings in Bioinformatics
  volume: '25'
  issue: '3'
  start: bbae122
  year: 2024
